<p>Use this function to embed a text and background pattern in confidential 
 documents. If an unauthorized copy of the document is made, the background 
 pattern and text will be clearly visible. This function makes it easy 
 to identify unauthorized copies.</p>
<p>If documents printed with <span class="Term-Soft">Unauthorized Copy Prevention 
 for Pattern</span> are copied, scanned, and/or stored, functions are disabled 
 in order to prevent information leakage.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you want the document image to be replaced 
 by a solid gray image when printed documents are scanned, copied, or sent 
 to the Document Server without permission, use the <a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_GUARD"><span class="Term-Soft">Data Security for Copying</span></a> function.</p></li>
<li><p>For details about the unauthorized copy prevention 
 function and effects, see the operating instructions provided with the 
 printer.</p></li>
<li><p>Printing with this function takes longer than 
 normal printing because more data is processed.</p></li>
<li><p>Depending on the unauthorized copy prevention 
 settings, the driver's prevention pattern may be overwritten by the printer's 
 pattern.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Unauthorized 
 Copy Prevention</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Unauthorized Copy 
 Prevention for Pattern</span> in <span class="Term-Soft">Unauthorized Copy 
 Prevention Type</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> 
 to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Unauthorized Copy Prevention for Pattern 
 Details</span> dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the text type for the prevention text in 
 the list.</p></li>
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">User Text</span> 
 in <span class="Term-Soft">Text Type:</span> list, enter a user text using 
 up to 64 single-byte characters.</p></li>
<li><p>To change the font, font style and font size, 
 specify from <span class="Term-Soft">Font:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Font 
 Style:</span> and <span class="Term-Soft">Size:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To change the angle, specify a value in <span class="Term-Soft">Angle:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a position to enter the prevention text 
 in <span class="Term-Soft">Position:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To repeat text, select the pattern in <span class="Term-Soft">Repeat:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Specify the line spacing in <span class="Term-Soft">Line 
 Space:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To print the text in outline form, select the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Outlined</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>To use only the text pattern when printing with 
 the unauthorized copy prevention, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Text 
 Only</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>To exchange the pattern of the text and the pattern 
 of the background, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Reverse Patterns (Text/Background)</span> 
 check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the mask type for the background pattern 
 in <span class="Term-Soft">Mask Type:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the density and color of the prevention 
 copy text/pattern in <span class="Term-Soft">Density:</span> and <span class="Term-Soft">Color:</span>.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">You can use 
 only black for monochrome printers.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="18">
<li><p>To exclude the specified area from being printed 
 with the pattern, select the <span class="Term-Soft">No Pattern Area:</span> 
 check box.<br/>
 Specify the values for <span class="Term-Soft">A:top</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">B:bttm</span>, 
 <span class="Term-Soft">C:left</span>, and <span class="Term-Soft">D:right</span> 
 in mm. The specified range is 1-9999 mm.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
